WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.481
Time Management.

2
00:00:01.761 --> 00:00:05.771
Day 61 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:07.521 --> 00:00:08.545
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.825 --> 00:00:23.289
Today's goal: prioritise your work, protect focus time, and, most importantly for communication, talk about time: giving realistic estimates, saying no, renegotiating deadlines and updating people before they have to ask.

5
00:00:24.639 --> 00:00:25.493
Part 1.

6
00:00:25.773 --> 00:00:28.482
Prioritise: the urgent, important grid.

7
00:00:29.732 --> 00:00:31.076
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:32.913
Urgent, and Not urgent.

9
00:00:33.193 --> 00:00:34.111
Important.

10
00:00:34.391 --> 00:00:35.244
Urgent:

11
00:00:35.524 --> 00:00:37.977
Do now: production incident, release blocker.

12
00:00:38.257 --> 00:00:39.260
Not urgent:

13
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.804
Schedule: design doc, learning, tech debt, one-on-ones.

14
00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:44.172
Not important.

15
00:00:44.452 --> 00:00:45.305
Urgent:

16
00:00:45.585 --> 00:00:48.807
Delegate or quick reply: most pings, some meetings.

17
00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:50.089
Not urgent:

18
00:00:50.369 --> 00:00:52.929
Drop: endless scrolling, optional meetings.

19
00:00:54.279 --> 00:00:57.351
Most real growth happens in important, not urgent.

20
00:00:57.631 --> 00:00:59.914
Block time for it, or it never happens.

21
00:01:01.264 --> 00:01:02.139
Part 2.

22
00:01:02.419 --> 00:01:03.976
Daily and weekly habits.

23
00:01:05.226 --> 00:01:08.661
Plan (5 min each morning): pick your top 3 for the day.

24
00:01:08.941 --> 00:01:10.029
Focus blocks:

25
00:01:10.309 --> 00:01:14.575
90 to 120 minutes, notifications off, calendar blocked.

26
00:01:14.855 --> 00:01:19.186
Batch small things: emails and Slack 3 to 4 times a day, not all day.

27
00:01:19.466 --> 00:01:23.946
End-of-day review: what's done, what moves to tomorrow, who needs an update.

28
00:01:24.226 --> 00:01:29.154
Weekly plan (Friday or Monday): priorities, deadlines, meetings to decline.

29
00:01:30.504 --> 00:01:31.400
Part 3.

30
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:32.853
Talking about time.

31
00:01:34.103 --> 00:01:35.085
Estimating.

32
00:01:35.365 --> 00:01:39.738
It'll take three to five days, assuming the API contract doesn't change.

33
00:01:40.018 --> 00:01:44.541
I need half a day to investigate before I can give you a reliable estimate.

34
00:01:44.821 --> 00:01:47.573
The fastest I can do with good quality is Thursday.

35
00:01:48.923 --> 00:01:50.821
Prioritising with your manager.

36
00:01:51.101 --> 00:01:52.040
You could say:

37
00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.760
I have three things this week: the search release, the bug from the client, and the hiring interviews.

38
00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.576
I can't do all three well.

39
00:01:59.856 --> 00:02:01.264
Which one should come first?

40
00:02:02.614 --> 00:02:04.065
Protecting focus time.

41
00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:06.883
I'm heads-down until 1 pm on the release.

42
00:02:07.163 --> 00:02:08.849
Can I get back to you after that?

43
00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.454
I've blocked 10 to 12 for focus time.

44
00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.206
Could we meet at 3 instead?

45
00:02:13.486 --> 00:02:16.259
Do you need me in this meeting, or can I read the notes?

46
00:02:17.609 --> 00:02:18.569
Running late.

47
00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:19.788
You could say:

48
00:02:20.068 --> 00:02:23.844
Heads-up: the report will be a day late, Thursday instead of Wednesday.

49
00:02:24.124 --> 00:02:26.663
The data export took longer than expected.

50
00:02:26.943 --> 00:02:28.521
Everything else is on track.

51
00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:32.961
Is Thursday morning okay, or should I send a partial version on Wednesday?

52
00:02:34.311 --> 00:02:37.255
Tell people as soon as you know, not on the deadline day.

53
00:02:38.605 --> 00:02:39.523
Part 4.

54
00:02:39.803 --> 00:02:41.723
Meetings: take back your calendar.

55
00:02:42.973 --> 00:02:44.210
Decline politely:

56
00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.770
Thanks for the invite.

57
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.949
I don't think I'm needed for this one.

58
00:02:48.229 --> 00:02:49.509
Could you share the notes?

59
00:02:49.789 --> 00:02:51.026
Ask for an agenda:

60
00:02:51.306 --> 00:02:53.631
Could you share an agenda so I can prepare?

61
00:02:53.911 --> 00:02:54.743
Shorten:

62
00:02:55.023 --> 00:02:57.733
Could we do this in 15 minutes instead of 30?

63
00:02:58.013 --> 00:02:58.823
Async:

64
00:02:59.103 --> 00:03:01.471
Could this be a Slack thread instead of a meeting?

65
00:03:02.821 --> 00:03:03.781
Part 5.

66
00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:06.301
Conversation: too many priorities.

67
00:03:07.551 --> 00:03:09.578
Here is how the conversation goes.

68
00:03:09.858 --> 00:03:11.394
Do you have ten minutes?

69
00:03:11.674 --> 00:03:13.999
I need help prioritising this week.

70
00:03:14.279 --> 00:03:14.983
Sure.

71
00:03:15.263 --> 00:03:16.501
What's going on?

72
00:03:16.781 --> 00:03:22.797
I've got the search release on Friday, the client bug, three interviews, and the architecture doc.

73
00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:24.186
That's a lot.

74
00:03:24.466 --> 00:03:25.639
What's at risk?

75
00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:28.589
The conversation continues.

76
00:03:28.869 --> 00:03:33.563
If I do everything, the release slips to Monday and the doc doesn't happen.

77
00:03:33.843 --> 00:03:36.253
The release and the client bug are the top two.

78
00:03:36.533 --> 00:03:38.539
Can someone else take one interview?

79
00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:40.163
Ravi offered to.

80
00:03:40.443 --> 00:03:43.216
And the architecture doc could move to next week.

81
00:03:43.496 --> 00:03:44.371
Agreed.

82
00:03:44.651 --> 00:03:48.043
Release first, then the bug, two interviews, and the doc next week.

83
00:03:49.393 --> 00:03:50.993
The conversation continues.

84
00:03:51.273 --> 00:03:52.083
Thanks.

85
00:03:52.363 --> 00:03:56.353
I'll update the interview panel and block focus time for the release.

86
00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:58.641
Part 6.

87
00:03:58.921 --> 00:03:59.839
Practice.

88
00:04:01.089 --> 00:04:05.825
List everything on your plate this week and put each item in the urgent, important grid.

89
00:04:06.105 --> 00:04:10.073
Then write the one message you need to send to renegotiate something.

90
00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:12.361
Part 7.

91
00:04:12.641 --> 00:04:13.687
Speak today.

92
00:04:14.937 --> 00:04:18.734
Block one 90-minute focus slot in your calendar for tomorrow.

93
00:04:19.014 --> 00:04:21.446
Decline or shorten one meeting politely.

94
00:04:21.726 --> 00:04:24.585
Give one estimate as a range with an assumption.

95
00:04:25.935 --> 00:04:27.471
That's the end of this lesson.

96
00:04:27.751 --> 00:04:32.401
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

97
00:04:32.681 --> 00:04:38.804
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

